sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CLI as cli/jobs.ts (jobs run)
    participant H as cli-handler.ts
    participant C as jobs-clock.ts
    participant S as jobs-state/NAME.state.json
    participant A as cli/jobs.ts (jobs attempt, detached)
    participant R as jobs-state/results/NAME.ID.NONCE.json
    participant LD as launchd entry (jobs launchd-run)
    participant X as jobs-state/results/NAME@SLOTMS.json

    Note over C: one tick a minute, one at a time, only while holding _daemon.lock<br/>each tick: apply results, then decide each runner=daemon job (backoff, needs, overlap), then alerts
    opt runner = launchd: launchd triggers, the daemon delivers
        LD->>X: at the slot (or once on wake): run the check, leave {slot, slotAt, result, output}, unless one waits already
        C->>X: applyExternal: oldest slot first, a slot at or below appliedExternal is a replay and is dropped
        alt nothing, failed, not now, or no target
            C->>S: record it at once, appliedExternal = slotAt, delete
        else output for a target
            C->>S: reserve a dispatch with external = slotAt (then the spawn below, with --external)
        end
    end
    alt tick: latest slot owed (runner = daemon)
        C->>S: reserve dispatch {id, nonce, at, kind: scheduled, slot, deadline} (sync, no await)
    else jobs run
        CLI->>H: jobs-run {name}
        H->>C: requestRun(name)
        C->>S: reserve dispatch {..., kind: manual} (same sync step: refuses "already running")
    end
    C->>A: spawn detached: jobs attempt PLATFORM NAME --dispatch --nonce --slot --slot-at [--external] [--manual] --state-dir<br/>stdin = job definition, stdout/stderr = NAME.log
    C->>S: add pid + lstart
    opt jobs run
        H-->>CLI: {id, pid, lstart}
        Note over CLI: Ctrl-C: SIGTERM to pid (not the group), only while lstart matches
    end
    A->>A: check, then action (2 min timeout), self-deadline 34 min awake. --external: no check, the action on the launchd output
    A->>R: write result once {dispatch, at, result, note}
    Note over A: deadline or SIGTERM: write first, then kill own group
    loop each tick
        C->>R: read result for the live dispatch
        alt result present
            C->>S: apply (idempotent via appliedDispatch), clear dispatch, and for external: appliedExternal = slotAt, delete NAME@SLOTMS
            C->>R: delete
        else pid gone (lstart mismatch) / no pid past grace and no orphan by argv
            C->>S: failure "ended without a result", appliedDispatch = id
        else alive past deadline
            C->>A: SIGTERM to the attempt, a grace later SIGKILL -pid (lstart re-checked)
        end
        C->>R: sweep results with id <= appliedDispatch
    end
    CLI->>S: poll until appliedDispatch >= id, print last/notNow tagged with id
